Unconstrained whole-number spelling defaults to `I32`. Decimal-point and
exponent spelling defaults to `F64`:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    score = 42
    ratio = 0.5
    population = 1e6
    temperature = -5
]

The grammar uses lowercase `e`, has no suffixes or radix forms and rejects
unary `+` and spaced `- count`. Small values do not infer narrow types.

An exact receiver materialises a literal directly:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    small U8 = 200
    large U64 = 18_000_000_000
    half F16 = 0.5
    price Dec2 = 12.50
]

An exact receiver can also type unresolved literal arithmetic:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    total U8 = 1 + 2
    money Dec4 = 0.1 + 0.2
]

The `U8` operation checks its own narrow result. A bound value keeps its type:
receiving context can type a raw literal beside it, but cannot retype that
named value or a completed operation. See @./#numeric-literals (Numeric
literals) for body-local inference, peer priority and barriers.
